    Explain that WhisperC++ autoencode is an Opencast feature (#6795)
    
    WhisperC++ now supports converting audio internally if built with FFmpeg
    support:
    
    https://github.com/ggml-org/whisper.cpp/blob/2679bec6e09231c6fd59715fcba3eebc9e2f6076/README.md#ffmpeg-support-linux-only
    
    That may make the auto encode option a bit confusing and we should
    explain that Opencast does the encoding and then passes the encoded file
    to WhisperC++.
    
